# netsurf: a flex or grid container's box-less child-list change and inert attributes need no rebuild (patch 408)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 407)
#
# The census's "nearest box is not a block" (8: stackoverflow 4, wpblog,
# wpnews, youtube). A debug build (scratch only): the change sat on a
# flex container itself -- a child-list change on stackoverflow's flex
# <body> (4), an inert attribute (patch 383's kind: aria-*, data-*, role)
# on wpblog's navigation <button> (2), another mark on youtube's <main>,
# a class change in an inline inside a flex <div>. The walk to the nearest
# block box declined on the flex box before any local answer could look.
#
#  - An inert attribute mark (html_rl_attr_mark_node: patch 310's gate let
#    it through -- no sheet, the UA's included, matches on it) on a box
#    that is not a block and holds no object, control, frame or list
#    marker: nothing to rebuild (383's no-op, any box type). Logged
#    "attribute on a box that is not a block, nothing to rebuild".
#  - A child-list mark on a flex or grid box: html_rl_block_change runs
#    with html_rl_noop_only -- patch 378's box-less no-op may answer, with
#    its structural and sibling checks; a change in elements with a box
#    declines (flex items need box_normalise_flex, which the block
#    placement does not do).
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-08 04:41:00.072403225 +0000
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-08 04:59:44.551674392 +0000
